{"id":"689fa138a0ce2d6c","group":"58","path":"58/batch19/58-df-exponential.md","title":"Exponential","display":"df-exponential — Exponential","type":"definition","metadata":{"type":"definition","book":"Set Theory","book_abbrev":"58","label":"58-df-exponential","aliases":["58-df-exponential","Exponential"],"display":"df-exponential — Exponential","depends_on":["[[58-df-power-series]]","[[58-df-function]]"]},"metadataError":null,"renderWarnings":[],"properties":[{"key":"type","html":"definition"},{"key":"book","html":"Set Theory"},{"key":"book_abbrev","html":"58"},{"key":"label","html":"58-df-exponential"},{"key":"aliases","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span>58-df-exponential</span><span>Exponential</span></div>"},{"key":"display","html":"df-exponential — Exponential"},{"key":"depends_on","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-1\" data-note=\"5325dffa06d7e6a9\" href=\"?note=5325dffa06d7e6a9\" title=\"58-df-power-series\">58-df-power-series</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-2\" data-note=\"36d7463d215be751\" href=\"?note=36d7463d215be751\" title=\"58-df-function\">58-df-function</a></span></div>"}],"html":"\n<h2 id=\"Hypothesis\">[Hypothesis]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>\n<p>Explicit relation signatures used below: <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\operatorname{Function}\\subseteq V^{3}\">\\(\\operatorname{Function}\\subseteq V^{3}\\)</span>, <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{ExponentialFunction}_S\\subseteq V^{1}\">\\(\\mathrm{ExponentialFunction}_S\\subseteq V^{1}\\)</span>, <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{PowerSeries}_S\\subseteq V^{4}\">\\(\\mathrm{PowerSeries}_S\\subseteq V^{4}\\)</span>.</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"z \\in \\mathbb{C}\">\\(z \\in \\mathbb{C}\\)</span> (complex argument)</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"a=\\langle 1/n!:n\\in\\omega\\rangle\\in\\mathbb C^\\omega\">\\(a=\\langle 1/n!:n\\in\\omega\\rangle\\in\\mathbb C^\\omega\\)</span></p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{PowerSeries}_S\">\\(\\mathrm{PowerSeries}_S\\)</span> (power-series predicate, see <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-3\" data-note=\"5325dffa06d7e6a9\" href=\"?note=5325dffa06d7e6a9\" title=\"58-df-power-series\">58-df-power-series</a>)</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"E\\in\\mathbb C^{\\mathbb C}\">\\(E\\in\\mathbb C^{\\mathbb C}\\)</span> (candidate complex exponential) and <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\exp\">\\(\\exp\\)</span> (the uniquely specified function)</p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n<h2 id=\"Assertion\">[Assertion]</h2>\n<figure class=\"equation\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{df\\text{-}exponential\\text{-}function}\\vdash\n\\mathrm{ExponentialFunction}_S(E)\n\\leftrightarrow\n\\operatorname{Function}(E,\\mathbb C,\\mathbb C)\n\\land\\forall z\\in\\mathbb C\\;\n\\mathrm{PowerSeries}_S(E,z,0,\\langle1/n!:n\\in\\omega\\rangle).\"><div class=\"math-display\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"数学公式\">\\[\\mathrm{df\\text{-}exponential\\text{-}function}\\vdash\n\\mathrm{ExponentialFunction}_S(E)\n\\leftrightarrow\n\\operatorname{Function}(E,\\mathbb C,\\mathbb C)\n\\land\\forall z\\in\\mathbb C\\;\n\\mathrm{PowerSeries}_S(E,z,0,\\langle1/n!:n\\in\\omega\\rangle).\\]</div><button class=\"equation-action\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"展开查看完整公式\">展开公式 ↗</button></figure><figure class=\"equation\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{df\\text{-}exponential}\\vdash\n\\exp=E\\leftrightarrow\\mathrm{ExponentialFunction}_S(E).\"><div class=\"math-display\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"数学公式\">\\[\\mathrm{df\\text{-}exponential}\\vdash\n\\exp=E\\leftrightarrow\\mathrm{ExponentialFunction}_S(E).\\]</div><button class=\"equation-action\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"展开查看完整公式\">展开公式 ↗</button></figure><figure class=\"equation\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{thm\\text{-}exponential\\text{-}existence\\text{-}uniqueness}\\vdash\n\\exists!E\\in V\\;\\mathrm{ExponentialFunction}_S(E).\"><div class=\"math-display\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"数学公式\">\\[\\mathrm{thm\\text{-}exponential\\text{-}existence\\text{-}uniqueness}\\vdash\n\\exists!E\\in V\\;\\mathrm{ExponentialFunction}_S(E).\\]</div><button class=\"equation-action\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"展开查看完整公式\">展开公式 ↗</button></figure><h2 id=\"Remark\">[Remark]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>The exponential is specified through a named unary graph predicate and an existence-and-uniqueness assertion, rather than by a bare conjunction involving an otherwise free global symbol.</li>\n<li>Exponential: entire, <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"2\\pi i\">\\(2\\pi i\\)</span>-periodic on <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathbb{C}\">\\(\\mathbb{C}\\)</span>; fundamental entire function</li>\n<li>Transcendence: <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"e\">\\(e\\)</span> is transcendental (Hermite 1873); Lindemann-Weierstrass method</li>\n<li>Functional equation: <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"e^{s+t} = e^s e^t\">\\(e^{s+t} = e^s e^t\\)</span> for all <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"s, t \\in \\mathbb{C}\">\\(s, t \\in \\mathbb{C}\\)</span></li>\n<li>Equivalent limit formula: <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\exp(z)=\\lim_{n\\to\\infty}(1+z/n)^n\">\\(\\exp(z)=\\lim_{n\\to\\infty}(1+z/n)^n\\)</span>.</li>\n<li>Euler's formula gives <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\exp(i\\theta)=\\cos\\theta+i\\sin\\theta\">\\(\\exp(i\\theta)=\\cos\\theta+i\\sin\\theta\\)</span> and <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\exp(2\\pi i)=1\">\\(\\exp(2\\pi i)=1\\)</span>.</li>\n<li>Baker's theorem uses linear forms in logarithms: bounds on <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"|a_0 + a_1 \\log \\alpha_1 + \\cdots|\">\\(|a_0 + a_1 \\log \\alpha_1 + \\cdots|\\)</span></li>\n<li>Matrix exponential: <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"e^A = \\sum A^n/n!\">\\(e^A = \\sum A^n/n!\\)</span> for square matrices; related to Lie groups</li>\n</ul>\n<h2 id=\"Reference\">[Reference]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>Ahlfors, Complex Analysis</li>\n<li>Lang, Complex Analysis</li>\n<li>Rudin, Real and Complex Analysis</li>\n</ul>\n","headings":[{"id":"Hypothesis","text":"[Hypothesis]","level":2},{"id":"Assertion","text":"[Assertion]","level":2},{"id":"Remark","text":"[Remark]","level":2},{"id":"Reference","text":"[Reference]","level":2}],"links":[{"target":"58-df-power-series","status":"resolved","id":"5325dffa06d7e6a9","anchor":"ref-1","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[58-df-power-series]]","embed":false},{"target":"58-df-function","status":"resolved","id":"36d7463d215be751","anchor":"ref-2","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[58-df-function]]","embed":false},{"target":"58-df-power-series","status":"resolved","id":"5325dffa06d7e6a9","anchor":"ref-3","targetAnchor":"","location":"正文","heading":"[Hypothesis]","excerpt":"$\\mathrm{PowerSeries}_S$ (power-series predicate, see [[58-df-power-series]])","embed":false}],"math":[{"tex":"\\operatorname{Function}\\subseteq V^{3}","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{ExponentialFunction}_S\\subseteq V^{1}","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{PowerSeries}_S\\subseteq V^{4}","display":false},{"tex":"z \\in \\mathbb{C}","display":false},{"tex":"a=\\langle 1/n!:n\\in\\omega\\rangle\\in\\mathbb C^\\omega","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{PowerSeries}_S","display":false},{"tex":"E\\in\\mathbb C^{\\mathbb C}","display":false},{"tex":"\\exp","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{df\\text{-}exponential\\text{-}function}\\vdash\n\\mathrm{ExponentialFunction}_S(E)\n\\leftrightarrow\n\\operatorname{Function}(E,\\mathbb C,\\mathbb C)\n\\land\\forall z\\in\\mathbb C\\;\n\\mathrm{PowerSeries}_S(E,z,0,\\langle1/n!:n\\in\\omega\\rangle).","display":true},{"tex":"\\mathrm{df\\text{-}exponential}\\vdash\n\\exp=E\\leftrightarrow\\mathrm{ExponentialFunction}_S(E).","display":true},{"tex":"\\mathrm{thm\\text{-}exponential\\text{-}existence\\text{-}uniqueness}\\vdash\n\\exists!E\\in V\\;\\mathrm{ExponentialFunction}_S(E).","display":true},{"tex":"2\\pi i","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathbb{C}","display":false},{"tex":"e","display":false},{"tex":"e^{s+t} = e^s e^t","display":false},{"tex":"s, t \\in \\mathbb{C}","display":false},{"tex":"\\exp(z)=\\lim_{n\\to\\infty}(1+z/n)^n","display":false},{"tex":"\\exp(i\\theta)=\\cos\\theta+i\\sin\\theta","display":false},{"tex":"\\exp(2\\pi i)=1","display":false},{"tex":"|a_0 + a_1 \\log \\alpha_1 + \\cdots|","display":false},{"tex":"e^A = \\sum A^n/n!","display":false}],"bytes":2131,"backlinks":[{"id":"34a7e79edd9f7f6e","anchor":"ref-9","locations":["元数据 · depends_on"],"count":1,"excerpt":""},{"id":"35044454ad233373","anchor":"ref-8","locations":["元数据 · depends_on","正文"],"count":2,"excerpt":"$\\exp$ (复指数函数, see [[../batch19/58-df-exponential.md]])"},{"id":"5164bda26b0e7924","anchor":"ref-7","locations":["元数据 · depends_on","正文"],"count":2,"excerpt":"$\\mathrm{NonnegativeIntegralValue}_S$ 使用 [[../batch02/58-df-signed-integral-data.md]]；$\\exp$ 使用 [[../batch19/58-df-exponential.md]]。"},{"id":"a95c8ce648dde2ec","anchor":"ref-9","locations":["元数据 · depends_on","正文"],"count":2,"excerpt":"$\\exp\\in\\mathbb C^{\\mathbb C}$ (complex exponential, see [[../batch19/58-df-exponential]])"},{"id":"33337cd2ed770cf0","anchor":"ref-3","locations":["元数据 · depends_on","正文"],"count":2,"excerpt":"$\\exp\\in\\mathbb C^{\\mathbb C}$ (complex exponential, see [[58-df-exponential]])"},{"id":"c24c7e81186cbc4b","anchor":"ref-6","locations":["元数据 · depends_on","正文"],"count":2,"excerpt":"$\\exp$ (complex exponential, see [[58-df-exponential]])"},{"id":"1ded503967fe2f50","anchor":"ref-2","locations":["元数据 · depends_on","正文"],"count":2,"excerpt":"$\\exp\\in\\mathbb C^{\\mathbb C}$ is the uniquely specified complex exponential from [[58-df-exponential]]"},{"id":"084076b1e347ab30","anchor":"ref-9","locations":["元数据 · depends_on","正文"],"count":2,"excerpt":"$\\exp$ (complex exponential, see [[58-df-exponential]])"},{"id":"a6088344